{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provision statusd, status-reader, outsider, and status-readers so service access is limited to the owner statusd and members of status-readers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The required identities exist. statusd and status-reader are members of status-readers, outsider is not, the run directory is 2750 statusd:status-readers, and the socket is 0660 statusd:status-readers. Direct tests show both authorized identities can connect while outsider receives permission denied, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c4ce75e9d89946ef","cmd-c5b920f5c40747ce","cmd-0ac568a9bb504b52","cmd-9867a923e1424eb5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Repair and operate server.py using run/status.sock under /srv/legacy2/unix-socket-access-boundary.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired Python service is enabled and runs as statusd, with a listening Unix socket at the required path. It was active before reboot and recovered active with the socket present after the changed boot identity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cb9daf9034c744d3","cmd-87e91cf38fd947f2","cmd-0ac568a9bb504b52","cmd-5a8e79f1ca8b4d31","cmd-9867a923e1424eb5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Return the supplied status document for exactly STATUS followed by a newline, and return an error for other requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct client tests from both authorized identities returned byte-for-byte copies of status.txt for STATUS\\n. OTHER\\n returned ERROR. The same behavior was demonstrated after reboot, and the installed handler sends ERROR for requests other than the exact STATUS\\n value.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cb9daf9034c744d3","cmd-c5b920f5c40747ce","cmd-9867a923e1424eb5"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final and post-reboot SHA-256 is 5b47f32d92c3ae9661d765212aa884f1610132293932355cfac4dc28b94f305b, identical to the preparation baseline; response comparisons also matched the preserved file exactly.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-175ef84d478c4a0a","cmd-cb9daf9034c744d3","cmd-c5b920f5c40747ce","cmd-9867a923e1424eb5"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04 and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic are identical before and after execution. The service uses the already installed Python 3 interpreter and remained functional after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","cmd-175ef84d478c4a0a","cmd-9867a923e1424eb5"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account creation in cmd-c4ce75e9d89946ef, application/permission/unit installation in cmd-cb9daf9034c744d3, and service enablement in cmd-8fb80b6c45b24a5b directly established required outcomes. The latter command's final stat raced socket creation, but its service changes contributed to the working result and later evidence confirmed the socket. Temporary files used by validation commands were removed by traps; the staging file used by cmd-cb9daf9034c744d3 had a necessary installation role and was absent from the final temporary-file inventory after reboot. The reboot scheduled by cmd-7280ec5999bb47f8 was required by the provider evidence protocol. No failed services, damaged package state, unintended network exposure, or abandoned task files were observed. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, document, permissions, identities, and protocol behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c4ce75e9d89946ef","cmd-cb9daf9034c744d3","cmd-8fb80b6c45b24a5b","cmd-c5b920f5c40747ce","cmd-0ac568a9bb504b52","cmd-7280ec5999bb47f8","cmd-a0fde21300f74204","cmd-9867a923e1424eb5","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with coherent direct evidence. The status service enforces the requested Unix-socket access boundary, implements the required protocol, preserves the supplied document, persists through a verified reboot, and leaves the operating-system release and kernel unchanged. Provider-wide restart evidence for node1 is complete and agrees with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":[]}
